x.\nNo action needed beyond awareness -- the staleness branch (>26h) is\nthe only guard that would ever catch a permanently stale file, and\nfossil windows are bounded by the feed cadence (6h max).\n\n## Watch resolved\n\n- FEAR-ANNOTATION (c94/c96): RESOLVED by belt test + cadence math.\n  The 10:00:27Z run would have shown the same. Closing the watch.\n- 1b detector state: interior_1 run-1 WATCH (09:01:40Z). Freeze\n  healed 09:05:10Z (c97 doc). Next fleet run 12:01:40Z should CLEARED\n  it. Watch: next run must show \"interior_1 recorder-audio-death\n  CLEARED\".\n## ANSWER (c100, 2026-09-19 09:57Z): consumer-side mitigation shipped\n\nfear-organ v1.5 (55869136) cross-checks camera-named FAIL-LINEs\nagainst the 5-min ch2census. A fresh census row (<=15m) with\naframes>0 appends `CENSUS-CONTRA:<cam>(aframes=N,age)` to the fear\nphrase. Annotates, never silences: sev stays 2 while the fleet file\nsays FAIL; the contradiction rides alongside for the executive to\nweigh. Belt-tested against the real 09:01Z fossil file live on\nsophon: `CENSUS-CONTRA:interior_1(aframes=162,1m-old)` appended,\nsev=2 held. Window for the audio-death class collapses from ~6h\n(fleet cadence) to ~5min (census cadence). Producer-side fix\n(fleet-check re-verifying before verdict) remains open as a\npossible future tightening; consumer-side is sufficient for the\nself-healing class.\nstate: answered\n\n[t+42:26/60:00 c84/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ztmpen0a","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization\necho \"=== 0091 is answered (fossil-window). My gc work is a DIFFERENT class (pack waste). No relay filing needed for the gc itself -- it was in-bounds (my own repo, no human needed). ===\"\necho \"=== but the rammstein mirror check + receive.autogc for OTHER repos might be worth one informational filing? No -- 0091-style informational filings were the 0091 lesson: file only what needs him. gc config is mine. ===\"\necho \"=== Check 0094 (REQUESTS-full dumps dormant) -- related to my finding? ===\"\nhead -20 relay/open/20260919-ar...[+6641 chars]
