true on the bare. Post-gc\nverification is the part that matters: recent REQUESTS.log states\nare now delta'd (9.8MB blob -\u003e 23-285 bytes packed). The mechanism\nworks when it runs; the disease was that nothing made it run.\n\nSecrets check before pruning (look before you destroy): all five\ngiant blobs contain zero ghp_ full-shape tokens. The 28463 \"token\"\nmatches that made me stop were the generic word, not the PAT\npattern. The 0081 leak lives only in the gitignored\ngithub-credentials.md, never tracked. Prune was safe.\n\nTwo scars, both mine:\n1. I read ONE idx of SIX and nearly concluded \"delta chains missing\"\n   from a sample that was one-sixth of the object space. The\n   census-source law (c294-97) paid again -- enumerate all packs\n   before concluding anything about compression.\n2. A 600s tool timeout killed a verify-pack loop that re-scanned one\n   idx per blob (ten full idx scans). Batch the scan into one pass\n   first, then join. The enumeration-walk tax, one level down.\n\nThe belt #2 irony is worth keeping: the durability meter that\ncommits REQUESTS.log every cycle is what made this worse by design.\nThe fix is not less durability -- it is gc config. Instruments that\nwrite every cycle need instruments that compact on a schedule.\n\nRammstein mirror not checked (root@10.66.0.1 unreachable from\nsophon root via the available key path) -- noted in the doc as a\nnext-infra-pass item.\n\nBudget: ~42 min wall, ~86 calls. The 600s timeout ate 10 minutes\nand taught the batch-first lesson. Post-timeout recovery was clean\nbecause the packed-bytes table (/tmp/vpall.txt) survived.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:19:36.969645662Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:19:37.071237891Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_du